parts.text:
Yes — and using it is more than a style choice: `propsWithDefaults` is already *shipped in ivue* and documented as the extensible-components doctrine, so the namespace-props idea should slot into that architecture rather than invent a parallel one. My inline `{ type: Number, default: 30 }` sketch was the naive version; the house version splits types from defaults, which is exactly what makes the horizontal override clean:

```ts
export namespace VirtualScroller {
  export const $Class = $VirtualScroller;
  export let Class = Reactive($Class) as unknown as typeof $VirtualScroller;
  export type Instance<T extends BaseItem> = ReactiveInstance<$VirtualScroller<T>>;

  /** Prop TYPES — the contract's shape */
  export const propsTypes = {
    modelValue: { type: Array as PropType<BaseItem[]>, required: true },
    assumedSize: { type: Number as PropType<number> },
    snapToItems: { type: Boolean as PropType<boolean> },
    creepMsPerPx: { type: Number as PropType<number> },
    /* … */
  };
  /** Prop DEFAULTS — plain values, factories auto-wrapped by the merge */
  export const propsDefaults = { assumedSize: 30, snapToItems: false /* … */ };
  export const props = propsWithDefaults(propsTypes, propsDefaults);
  export type Props<T extends BaseItem> = VirtualScrollerProps<T>;
}
```

And the horizontal variant becomes the textbook extension — redefine only what differs:

```ts
export namespace HorizontalVirtualScroller {
  export const props = propsWithDefaults(
    { ...VirtualScroller.propsTypes },
    { ...VirtualScroller.propsDefaults, assumedSize: 300 },
  );
}
```

Two properties make this safe where my sketch wasn't: `propsWithDefaults` is **non-mutating by contract** (that's a paid-for LESSONS entry — the mutating version once rewrote the *base* component's defaults through the spread, and the spec now pins copy-semantics), so the horizontal override can never bleed into the vertical scroller; and object/array defaults get auto-wrapped in factories, so nobody re-learns Vue's shared-reference default trap. Emits ride along the same way with `ExtractEmitTypes` per the same doc page.

So the synthesis of the whole discussion: **the namespace carries the full component contract** — `$Class` / `Class` / `Instance` / `propsTypes` / `propsDefaults` / `props` / `Props<T>` — built from the already-proven primitives (`propsWithDefaults`, `ExtractEmitTypes`), not new machinery. The extensible-components pattern and the namespace pattern stop being two conventions and become one.

Plan unchanged otherwise: ① scroller SFCs onto namespace-props + the `creepMsPerPx` seam, ② `BlogDripShowcase` → class (+ scrollbar handlers into the scroller class), ③ `TextChunker` (Static, pure) + `TextMarquee` (Reactive) + playground demo with speed setting, ④ live drive + docs. Say go.

